From fda8866b6ce48c2a7b4b0d019c7a9b1bd467532d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sudoom <20szynkarka_skrzywiony@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 20:07:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [cert-manager] Bump to 1.20

cert-manager 1.18 supports Kubernetes 1.29-1.33 and went EOL on 2026-03-10.
OKD 4.21 is Kubernetes 1.34, so the operator built from this branch is out of
its supported range on the OKD version it ships with.

1.20 covers Kubernetes 1.32-1.35, which spans OKD 4.19 through 4.22 -- one bump
clears both the current 4.21 and the upcoming 4.22, with no follow-up needed.

The OKDify patch had to be regenerated: its context included
'olm.skipRange: >=1.18.0 <1.18.1', so 'git am -3' failed against the 1.20 CSV
base with "sha1 information is lacking or useless". The regenerated patch makes
the same eight substitutions and applies cleanly.

Refs: https://cert-manager.io/docs/releases/
